# False positives, scoped to exact fingerprints (file:rule:line).
# The generic-api-key rule flags the CloudFormation parameter *names*
# "ExistingSubnet1Id" / "ExistingSubnet2Id" as high-entropy strings. They are
# parameter keys in an example params file, not secrets. Placeholder resource
# IDs in these files use the canonical AWS -0123456789abcdef0 form, which the
# gitleaks config allowlists. Scoped to these two lines only, so any new finding
# elsewhere still fails the gate.
params/containers-ecs-ec2-fsxn-nfs.example.json:generic-api-key:11
params/containers-ecs-ec2-fsxn-nfs.example.json:generic-api-key:15
